and anti-corruption laws in other jurisdictions;
• tighter restrictions on privacy and the collection and use of patient data;
• the impact of BREXIT on regulatory standards and operations; and
• business interruptions resulting from geopolitical actions (including war and terrorism), pandemic diseases
(such as the recent spread of COVID-19 “coronavirus”), or natural disasters (including earthquakes, typhoons,
floods and fires).
